API Share changes preserve JSON number precision, convert legacy functions
without double-prefixing, keep unknown response names unchanged, and integrate
with the gateway's native and converted JSON/SSE response paths. Local streaming
modifications assemble tool-name fragments with bounded state and preserve
arbitrary tool inputs. The captured prompt/tool assets retain the source
revision listed above.

Client tool names additionally follow upstream commit
4a4db10387ac6272c1e1ce754400870eed9c29f8 (2026-10-29, PR #161):
an ordinary tool namespace plus the first twelve hex characters of the name's
SHA-256. The request-local reverse map, schemas and descriptions remain intact;
original tool names do not survive in tool-name fields sent to the upstream.

Compatibility was checked against upstream v1.5.0, revision
e2b2a7c28114d08a28cc5250ae7d4c0a2b16f470 (2026-11-18), on 2026-11-19:
- 95575c5fd66327645d53e88c969037bb22a96be3 (#182): ordinary tool namespace.
- 87e798318d370a2ac9dcdf88a09fb21a9b7bbe27 (#166): restore official tool
  aliases to declared equivalents, remove undeclared history calls and paired
  results, and hold argument fragments while a Chat tool name is incomplete.
- internal/protocol/tools.go: resolve unique case/separator variants without
  guessing between ambiguous declarations. Unlike upstream's fallback, unknown
  prefixed names are preserved, not stripped blindly.
- internal/gateway/title.go and the classification ordering in 14faec7:
  recognize tool-free OpenCode title requests before prompt injection and
  skip completing their agent tool set; adapt system/instructions and input
  content for native Anthropic and Responses requests as well.

Local history handling also covers legacy Chat function calls/results and
Responses custom-tool outputs, while retaining scalar Responses input. Held
Chat names and arguments are flushed at a completed finish/DONE event or clean
event-boundary EOF; a missing terminator still reports an unexpected EOF.
